From 2379f8db7c927678845f6f85df515697b5800345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:12:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/gn: no ANGLE X11/Wayland WSI for Linux target builds

An embedder-only build for --target-os linux still evaluates
//flutter/third_party/angle, whose angle_use_wayland defaults to is_linux,
while Flutter's build_overrides/wayland.gni defines no wayland_dir, so gn
gen fails. Host (desktop) builds already turn these ANGLE options off; do
the same for explicit Linux target builds.

After ardera/flutter-ci's patch of the same name (MIT), adapted to this
revision.
---
 engine/src/flutter/tools/gn | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engine/src/flutter/tools/gn b/engine/src/flutter/tools/gn
index 7a2b89e..1b8554d 100755
--- a/engine/src/flutter/tools/gn
+++ b/engine/src/flutter/tools/gn
@@ -799,7 +799,9 @@ def to_gn_args(args):
   # There is a special case for Android on Windows because there we _only_ build
   # gen_snapshot, but the build defines otherwise make it look like the build is
   # for a host Windows build and make GN think we will be building ANGLE.
-  if is_host_build(args) or (args.target_os == 'android' and get_host_os() == 'win'):
+  if is_host_build(args) or args.target_os == 'linux' or (
+      args.target_os == 'android' and get_host_os() == 'win'
+  ):
     # Don't include git commit information.
     gn_args['angle_enable_commit_id'] = False
     # Do not build unnecessary parts of the ANGLE tree.
